      "text": "Let us start by taking the derivative of ( 3 x^{3} - 3 x^{2} + 11 x - 8 = 0 ):\n( 9 x^{2} - 6 x + 11 = 0 )\nWe are interested in finding:\n( h'left(a right) + h'left(b right) + h'left(c right) ).\nThe derivative of ( h(x) ) is obtained by applying the rules of integral calculus. Specifically:\n[ h'(x) = frac{d}{dx} left( frac{3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8}{3x - 1} right) ]\nTo clearly illustrate the fundamental and sequential steps of finding the derivative:\n1. Take the derivative of each factor ( 3x^3, -3x^2, 11x, -8 ) using the power rule: ( frac{d}{dx} (3x^n) = 3n x^{n-1} )\n   [ frac{d}{dx} (3x^3) = 9x^2 ]\n   [ frac{d}{dx} (-3x^2) = -6x ]\n   [ frac{d}{dx} (11x) = 11 ]\n   [ frac{d}{dx} (-8) = 0 ]\n2. Sum up these derivatives together.\nSo, the derivative of ( frac{3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8}{3x - 1} ) gives:\n( frac{d}{dx} left( frac{3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8}{3x - 1} right) = 9x^2 - 6x + 11 ).\nSince ( h'(x) ) as a function:\n( h'left(xright) = 9x^2 - 6x + 11 )\nAnd the goal we need is the value at ( x = a ), ( x = b ), and ( x = c ); substituting x by ( a ), ( b ), and ( c ) respectively through, a couple substitutions (such as into 5 ^2 {} - 6 times 5 {} + 11 ):\n( h'left(a right) = 5 {}^2 - 6 times 5 {} + 11 )\n( h'left(b right) = 5 {}^2 - 6 times 5 {} + 11 )\n( h'left(c right) = 5 {}^2 - 6 times 5 {} + 11 )\nThen the result for ( ab + ac + bc ) will be ( sum{}_{i=1}^{n} (h'(a_i)) ):\n( h'(a_1) + h'(a_2) + · · · + h'(a_n) = left( 5 {}^2 - 6 times 5 {} + 11 right) + left( 5 {}^2 - 6 times 5 {} + 11 right) + · · · + left( 5 {}^2 - 6 times 5 {} + 11 right) )\nThe conclusion is, given the values of the curve's points:\n[ h(a) = frac{ 3a^3 - 3a^2 + 11a - 8 }{3a - 1} = 5 {}^2 - 6 times 5 {} + 11 ]\nhence,\n[ h' left( a right) = 9 a^2 - 6 a + 11 ]\nSimilarly,\n[ h(b) = frac{ 3b^3 - 3b^2 + 11b - 8 }{3b - 1} = 5 {}^2 - 6 times 5 {} + 11 ]\ngives ( h'(b) ) and:\n[ h(c) = frac{ 3c^3 - 3c^2 + 11c - 8 }{3c - 1} = 5 {}^2 - 6 times 5 {} + 11 ]\ngives ( h'(c) ).\nAdding up:\n[ h'(a) + h'(b) + h'(c) = (h'(5 {} + (-15 )^2 + 11 ) + ≤br> h'(5 {} + (-15 )^2 + 11 ).\nTo finalize, feel free to refer to the full reasoning steps:\n\n( h'left(a right) + h'left(b right) + h'left(c right) ).\n\nTherefore, the solution is:\n[ h'left(a right) + h'left(b right) + h'left(c right) = (3a^3 - 3a^2 + 11a - 8)' / (3a - 1) evaluated at a, b, and c = h'(a) + h'(b) + h'(c) ]",
